<Text title="About us | thetoolproject" description="Learn why thetoolproject makes free, open source browser tools and how you can help improve them." heading="About thetoolproject" lead="Useful file tools should be easy to use and easy to trust." path="/about/">
  <p>thetoolproject.com makes small, focused tools for the file tasks that interrupt your day. Convert JSON to HTML or Excel, turn a spreadsheet into CSV, and get on with your work.</p>
  <p>The tools run in your browser. Your files and pasted data stay on your device during conversion, so you can use the tools without uploading a document or creating an account.</p>

  <h2>Built in the open</h2>
  <p>The project is <a href="https://github.com/harshit-dixit/thetoolproject.com">open source on GitHub</a>. You can read the code, suggest a change, or contribute under the repository’s <a href="https://github.com/harshit-dixit/thetoolproject.com/blob/main/LICENSE">MIT License</a>.</p>

  <h2>Help make the tools better</h2>
  <p>If something fails, a result looks wrong, or a file format is missing, <a href="https://github.com/harshit-dixit/thetoolproject.com/issues">open an issue</a>. For questions you would rather send privately, <a href="mailto:hello@thetoolproject.com">email us</a>.</p>
</Text>
